From fe70b06c8e977ccbd9ea8491b61cfd094fefbb9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiming Pang <discrete_brain@163.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 14:58:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/43] feat(smap): add bloom filter to skip cold PMDs during
 PTE scan

Borrow the PMD-level bloom filter pattern from MGLRU's aging walk
to reduce scan cost. The filter marks PMDs that had hot pages last
round; subsequent rounds only walk marked PMDs. A force_scan runs
every N rounds (default 4) to discover newly-hot PMDs.

- SMAP_BLOOM_FILTER_* constants: 4096-bit (512-byte) per-process filter
- smap_pmd_entry: .pmd_entry callback returns 1 to skip cold PMDs
  via the existing walk_page_range() infrastructure
- update_bloom_filter() in check_pte_young(): marks PMD on hot page
- smap_bloom_force_scan_interval module param (default 4)
- Bloom filter only active for NORMAL_SCAN; helpers safely no-op
  when filter is NULL for other scan types

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
